# 6. Fix-Version Evaluation

## Current Problem

Some commits are reported as violations because the story extracted from the commit message does not belong to the current fix version.

This is not sufficient to explain every violation.

A story may belong to:

- Current fix version.
- Previous fix version.
- Future fix version.
- Another release.
- No known fix version.

## Requirement

During commit analysis, determine the actual fix version associated with the extracted story.

The existing story lookup already retrieves information such as Scrum Team.

Extend the lookup so that the evaluated fix version is also available.

Do NOT overwrite the existing primary/current fix-version field if it has a different business purpose.

Add a separate DB field for the evaluated story fix version.

Suggested field name:

`evaluated_fix_version`

Before implementing, verify the existing schema/naming conventions and use the appropriate naming convention if another name is more consistent.

---

# 7. Violation Reason Classification

For each commit whose story does not belong to the current fix version, determine and persist the reason.

At minimum distinguish:

### Previous Fix Version

The story belongs to an earlier release/fix version.

### Current Fix Version

The story belongs to the currently analyzed fix version.

### Future Fix Version

The story belongs to a future release.

### Unknown / Unavailable

The story/fix-version information cannot be determined.

Use the actual Jira/iTrack data rather than guessing from version names.

Persist the evaluated fix version so that the UI can explain the violation accurately.

